new file mode 100644
index 000000000..fb1c46f3f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/peer_download_test/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# Socket-free bounded block download coordinator
+
+This candidate coordinates explicitly requested V2 blocks using the existing
+native peer codecs. It selects no network/profile, opens no sockets, changes no
+shared CMake/dispatcher, advertises no service and owns no persistent chain index.
+It is a single-owner scheduler; enclosing code serializes all calls.
+
+## API and callbacks
+
+Construct `DownloadManager` with explicit `DownloadConfig` and all four required
+callbacks. Zero/inconsistent limits and unbounded sentinel values reject with
+`invalid_argument`. There are no local policy or network defaults. Register only
+sessions that have completed V2 negotiation, using their negotiated limit.
+Registration returns checked monotonically allocated handles; a disconnected
+handle is never reused. Runtime registers each physical connection exactly once
+and retains that handle; registering the same connection again would bypass its
+lifecycle guards. `NextPeerHandle` exposes the checked boundary primitive.
+
+`RequestBlock` takes the exact expected native header and full/compact choice.
+It derives BlockID and checks contextual header eligibility before requesting
+body data. Missing parents produce `NeedHeaders` with the parent ID. Deferred
+requests are bounded jobs holding a fixed header, not peer body buffers.
+
+`OnMessage` borrows a complete, bounded Session application message. Full blocks,
+compact blocks, missing responses and notfound are associated with registered
+peer handle and requested BlockID. Unsolicited/late responses create no jobs and
+cannot modify another request. Compact requests permit a complete-block reply.
+The manager's only outbound records are single-item getdata and getblocktxn;
+the enclosing runtime encodes their TCP envelopes and owns a bounded send queue.
+
+`PollTimeout` processes at most one due job. Call it until Idle under a bounded
+runtime work budget. Deadlines use injected monotonic milliseconds and checked
+arithmetic. Duplicate/unknown traffic does not extend deadlines. Missing-index
+and full fallback phases get their configured phase deadline, capped by the
+original lifecycle deadline. Deferred retry never extends its expiry.
+
+`Cancel`, `OnReorg` and `OnDisconnect` release work. Reorg advances the caller's
+context generation and immediately clears every job, with a bounded affected-ID
+list and no hidden retry queue. Disconnect also releases that connection's
+retired guards. The manager does not select branches or mutate active-tip state.
+
+Callback outcomes are typed, never inferred from diagnostic strings:
+
+- Header: Eligible, MissingParent, Deferred, ConsensusInvalid, Unsupported,
+  OperationalError.
+- Body: Accepted, MalformedBody, ConsensusInvalid, MissingParent, Deferred,
+  CapacityRefused, Unsupported, StorageError, ContextChanged.
+- Reservation: Granted, CapacityRefused, OperationalError.
+
+Full and reconstructed complete bytes enter the same synchronous admission
+callback under a live reservation. Accepted means whatever atomic admission
+contract the enclosing validator explicitly supplies. The coordinator itself
+implements no VM, monetary transition, disk publication or rollback. In
+particular, an admission exception or StorageError can occur after an external
+commit: reconcile the authoritative tip/context before continuing. An operational
+failure is not proof that chain state stayed unchanged.
+
+Missing-parent/deferred complete bodies remain under their existing lease in a
+bounded deferred job. Retry rechecks header eligibility and calls admission
+again; timeout, reorg, cancellation and disconnect discard them. Header/body
+unsupported and operational outcomes remain distinct from consensus rejection.
+The manager has no permanent-invalid cache and emits ConsensusRejected only for
+an explicit corresponding callback result. Bad compact root/size/matching never
+produces that result by itself.
+
+## Reservations, cache and lifecycle bounds
+
+Explicit limits bound registered peers, jobs per peer/globally, deferred jobs,
+retired lifecycle guards per peer/globally, serialized staging bytes, transaction
+slots, cache candidates/cache bytes and all deadlines. Configuration must permit
+at least one worst-case job. Input Session buffers, output/event queues,
+validator scratch/UTXO backend caches and disk overlays have separate enclosing
+runtime budgets.
+
+A reservation is acquired before decoding transactions, reading cache candidates
+or retaining body copies. `ResourceNeed` is a conservative serialized staging
+and transaction-slot allowance, not a measured equal resident-memory ceiling:
+
+- Full mode reserves `4 * peer_payload_limit` staging bytes and
+  `4 * floor(peer_payload_limit / 17)` transaction slots. Seventeen bytes is the
+  existing full codec's conservative minimum framed transaction bound.
+- Compact mode reserves the maximum of that full allowance and
+  `4 * max_reconstruction_bytes + 2 * peer_payload_limit + cache_bytes`, with
+  the maximum of the full slots and `4 * max_reconstruction_transactions`.
+  Thus both an immediate full reply and later full fallback fit the original
+  lease. The bound covers simultaneously retained serialization/decoded copies;
+  it never allocates from an unchecked advertised Header.size.
+
+`CachedTransactions` supplies a borrowed flat span and its canonical total wire
+bytes. The callback must supply an already validated, bounded cache snapshot,
+not an unbounded query that allocates a new cache. Its span and transaction
+contents remain stable until `CompactReconstruction::Start` returns. The manager
+checks candidate count/declared bytes before scanning, then performs a bounded,
+allocation-free size/count preflight and verifies that metadata. Oversized cache
+views fall back to full retrieval; invalid/stale local metadata is operational,
+never a peer or consensus invalidity. No cache pointer survives Start.
+
+Granted leases are move-only RAII objects whose destructors must not throw.
+Whole-operation guards reject mutating reentry from callbacks or lease
+destructors with OperationalFailure. Allocation/length exceptions outside
+callback catches propagate after the unwinding guard aborts the peer's jobs,
+releases leases and disables further work on that handle. A global-operation
+unwind aborts all jobs. Retired guards survive; the enclosing runtime closes
+sessions and calls OnDisconnect (or destroys the manager). It must not reinterpret
+allocation failure as bad consensus data. Large temporary objects are released
+before their job lease; reserved counters release exactly once on terminal paths.
+
+Every issued peer/BlockID lifecycle retains a small guard until that connection
+disconnects. Timeout/cancel/reorg/completion drop heavy state but never permit a
+second missing request for that connection/ID. Compact-to-full is one transition
+within the existing job, and full retrieval is attempted at most once. Repeated
+compact/new-nonce responses cannot replace its request list. At guard quotas,
+refuse new lifecycles or rotate/disconnect the connection; do not evict guards
+and reuse the same connection/ID. Guard maps are explicitly bounded globally.
+
+Capacity refusal is recoverable. Tiny valid negotiated limits may not fit the
+37-byte single-item getdata. Compact resource/collision/root failures produce
+one full fallback where the complete body fits, otherwise RetryElsewhere.
+Typed fallback causes distinguish compact/cache/request capacity from generic
+reconstruction fallback. No vector is truncated. `notfound` carries no remote
+absence-versus-capacity reason, so the manager reports alternate-peer recovery
+without inventing one. Batched notices are bounded by existing job quotas.
+
+## Validation evidence and scope
+
+Standalone target:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S src/lotus_v2/peer_download_test -B /tmp/v2-peer-download-build -GNinja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
+  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/absolute/path/to/libsecp256k1.a
+cmake --build /tmp/v2-peer-download-build
+ctest --test-dir /tmp/v2-peer-download-build --output-on-failure
+```
+
+Add `-DLOTUS_SANITIZE=ON` for AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. The
+standalone target compiles inherited SHA256/SipHash, native codecs/signing and
+`support/cleanse.cpp`; Chronik and synthetic hashing overrides are absent.
+
+Debug and sanitizer checks pass in the isolated 2026-10-15 packet. Tests use
+real native full/compact framing and independently instrumented scheduling,
+reservation and admission callbacks. The test admission adapter checks complete
+framing/ordered roots; it is explicitly not native VM/state/monetary acceptance.
+Coverage includes exact full/compact bytes, peer/BlockID association, partial
+cache overlap, missing indices, duplicate-short-ID fallback and valid full-body
+recovery, cache count refusal before scanning invalid entries, capacity/size
+mismatch, every typed outcome, deadlines, cancellation/reorg, missing-parent and
+deferred-body recovery, per-peer/global job/byte/slot/guard/deferred quotas,
+notfound batches, callback/release reentry, handle/deadline overflow, exact lease
+cleanup and 220 deterministic allocator fault positions through compact work.
+Global reorg allocation failure also releases all queued jobs immediately.
+
+Remaining integration is explicit: activated-session ownership, actual peer
+selection/diversity, header synchronization and authenticated eligibility,
+validated body availability/serving, full-TxHash transaction relay, near-tip and
+anti-amplification policy, persistent index/atomic admission adapters, resource
+measurements, runtime retries/connection rotation, sockets, RPC and reviewed
+network/profile adoption. No public readiness, universal P05 delivery or daemon
+acceptance claim follows from this coordinator packet.
